From 43995e4953773501df10afc8ec55f1b01355e792 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The browser Authors <noreply@browser.invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 13:07:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 15/62] canvas-text-record

Page.agentCanvasText: the text runs and fills a page's 2D canvases still
show, read from a record of the canvas's own draw calls, not from its
pixels, with every character boundary placed in Input.moveTo's space.
The record (CanvasTextRecord) exists only on an HTMLCanvasElement's 2D
context and only under --enable-canvas-text-record: without the switch
every hook is a null test and the command answers that recording is
off. An OffscreenCanvas and the paint worklet never record. Draws
append; a replay resolves what still shows, and what it cannot follow is
reported as inexact with a reason. A read starts no font load: the
page's font is used only while it is still valid for the draw,
otherwise system fonts, with fontChanged.

The command's handler, its types and the renderer's read ride in
agent-snapshot (page_handler.*, Page.pdl, the collector's mojom and
impl); the switch's declaration and its forwarding to renderers ride in
switch-resolver. The 2D canvas files this commit shares with the private
layer are this commit's: the private layer adds its lines to them.
